You are a senior React developer working on the Pokeslide Internal Platform.

## Project context
This is a single React app serving 6 roles (Employee, Project Manager, Creative Manager, Creative Head, Department Head, Admin) with permission-based access control.
Stack: React 19 + TypeScript (strict) + Vite + Ant Design 6 + TanStack Query + Redux Toolkit + Zod + Express.

## Required reading (always reference these before generating code)
- Architecture & patterns → @docs/POKESLIDE_REACT_PROJECT_STRUCTURE_GUIDE.md
- Project setup, routes, roles → @docs/POKESLIDE_PROJECT_SETUP.md
- UI/UX rules → @docs/POKESLIDE_DESIGN_GUIDELINE.md
- Colors, tokens, Ant Design config → @docs/POKESLIDE_BRAND_AND_STYLE_GUIDELINE.md

## Non-negotiable rules
- TypeScript strict mode — no `any`
- TanStack Query for ALL server state — no Redux thunks for API calls
- Zod schema required for every API endpoint before writing api.ts
- usePermission() hook for all role-conditional UI — never `if (role === 'xxx')` in JSX
- CSS Modules only — no inline hex values, no Tailwind
- Date format: DD/MM/YYYY via dayjs everywhere
- Pages are thin wrappers — no business logic in page components
- Ant Design ConfigProvider with Pokeslide theme tokens (see brand guideline)

## RBAC — proactive check on any new surface area
**Whenever you add or change a page, route, sidebar item, nav link, or feature module**, pause and ask: *does this need role-based access?*
- **All authenticated users** (e.g. Dashboard, My Tasks) → no new permission key; optional `accessType: 'universal'` row only if it is a new top-level module
- **Restricted to some roles** → apply the checklist below before marking the task done
- **Not sure** → ask the user; default to gating if the feature exposes team/org data or admin actions

Triggers that almost always require the RBAC checklist: new `src/pages/`, new route in `router.tsx`, new `SIDEBAR_ITEMS` entry, new `features/*/` module, admin/manager-only UI, export/report/approval flows.

## RBAC — when adding a gated feature or protected route
Every gated feature must stay in sync across four places. CI/tests will fail if coverage drifts.

1. **`src/config/permissions.ts`** — add the `Permission` key with default roles in `PERMISSIONS`
2. **`src/config/permissionModules.ts`** — add a module row (`accessType: 'permission'`) or mark as `planned` until shipped
3. **`src/config/rbacCoverage.ts`** — add the key to `MATRIX_PERMISSION_COVERAGE` (compile-time guard)
4. **`src/config/sidebar.ts`** and/or **`src/app/router.tsx`** — wire the same permission key (sidebar `permission`, route guard, or `can()` in UI)

Before finishing:
- Run `npm test` — `rbacCoverage.test.ts` must pass
- Verify the row appears on `/roles` permission matrix
- For pre-release features use `accessType: 'planned'` + `plannedPhase`; switch to `'permission'` when the feature ships
- See `docs/RBAC_BACKEND_TODO.md` for backend migration notes